[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.9]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (A) at (0:2.4);
\coordinate (B) at (128:2.4);
\fill[blue!25] (O) -- (128:2.4) arc[start angle=128,end angle=360,radius=2.4] -- cycle;
\draw (O) -- (A);
\draw (O) -- (B);
\draw (128:2.4) arc[start angle=128,end angle=360,radius=2.4];
\pic[draw,"$128^{\circ}$",angle radius=0.7cm,angle eccentricity=2.1] {angle=A--O--B};
\fill (O) circle (1.6pt);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The marked angle is the **exterior** angle of the shaded sector.
What is the interior angle of the sector?

